agnitude is tiny relative to the outcome standard deviation and only marginal in a multiplicity-rich discovery setting, so I do not accept the original directional claim or its reversal as scientifically meaningful. H49, H50, H51, and H53 are all close to null: KIF18A/MSI-high, RIT1/KRAS in BRAF-wild-type cells, RPL11/MYC amplification within high MYC expression, and TMED10/ERBB2 amplification show intervals crossing zero with very small point estimates. I also reassess the original EGFR claim H3 using the overall borderline result plus the KRAS-wild-type and KRAS/BRAF-wild-type conditional null checks. Given that the overall estimate is small, its interval includes zero, and the mechanistically motivated conditional analyses are also null, H3 is rejected and closed as an unsupported dataset association. The strongest currently supported associations remain the very large TP53-wild-type/USP7, SMARCA4-loss/SMARCA2, MSI-high/WRN, and KEAP1-loss/weak-NFE2L2 effects, plus the robustness checks in adenocarcinoma and TP53-wild-type subsets for the NFE2L2 and WRN claims. Because H13 is large but directionally counterintuitive, I request independent validation for H13. These remain associations within the supplied dataset, not causal effects or externally generalizable clinical claims.",
