  "narrative": "The new validation results materially strengthen the leading claims. All estimates are already signed to the registered hypothesis direction: for direction -1, a positive estimate means stronger dependency/more negative score in the exposed group; for direction +1, a positive estimate means weaker dependency/less negative score in the exposed group.\n\nH7 is independently validated. The discovery result for SMARCA4-loss cells having stronger SMARCA2 dependency was +0.784 with a 95% discovery interval +0.765 to +0.803; validation gave +0.805 with an independent interval +0.774 to +0.836. The two estimates are nearly identical and both are extremely large relative to the SMARCA2 dependency-score scale. I therefore keep H7 accepted and close its investigation.\n\nH13 is now independently validated. This is the reversed, biologically counterintuitive claim that KEAP1-loss cells have weaker NFE2L2 dependency, i.e. a higher/less negative dependency_NFE2L2 score. Discovery was +0.796; validation was +0.802 with an independent interval +0.775 to +0.829. Because H10 was the original opposite-direction claim, validation evidence also strengthens rejection of H10. Thus H13 is accepted and closed as a dataset-supported association, while H10 remains rejected and closed. This does not imply causality or biological generality; it means the measured direction is consistent under independent validation in this dataset.\n\nH17 is independently validated. The WRN/MSI-high association, restricted to a comparator population with mutation burden at least 4, was +0.787 in discovery and +0.819 in validation with an independent interval +0.769 to +0.868. This supports the interpretation that the WRN association is not merely an artifact of comparing MSI-high cells against very low-mutation-burden cells. It also indirectly supports H9, but H9 itself is the unrestricted MSI-high effect and has not yet received direct independent validation, so I leave H9 accepted but active a